      <description>It’s a familiar sight across Mexico’s urban landscape: cities every time more congested, with inadequate public transportation and tortuous journeys from one end to the other. Traffic is a problem across Latin America and beyond, but Mexico City has more than earned its rank by some measures as the world’s most congested city.</description>
